AMENDMENT 2 to the freeze — 2026-08-28. Digest on line 1 is this amendment's.
Amendment 1's digest was d35ada6abc197b7b...
================================================================================

WHAT CHANGED, and nothing else changed:
  registry/reason_codes.json      454 -> 455 codes; registry_version 2 -> 3
                                  + PLATFORM.ADAPTER_BUSY (TRANSIENT, WARN,
                                    terminal false, not user_actionable,
                                    evidence errno/syscall/os_error_code/platform)
  tests/test_registries.py        asserts reason registry_version 3

  NO .proto changed. NO .cddl changed. contracts/gen/** is byte-identical.
  The OTHER THREE registries are untouched and stay at registry_version 2.
  Version parity was Amendment 1's convenience, not a rule; bumping an
  unchanged registry would claim a change a reader could not find.

WHY IT IS A DEFECT AND NOT AN INCONVENIENCE (§3 step 1):
  This is finding W-40 in docs/implementation/ownership.md §8, whose disposition
  said it would travel with W-18 to Amendment 1. IT DID NOT, and the register was
  wrong to imply otherwise — checked against all 454 codes, in all sixteen
  domains, not only PLATFORM.

  The seam reports a transient syscall outcome as PlatformError::Transient, which
  maps onto PLATFORM.ADAPTER_UNAVAILABLE — registered PERSISTENT, terminal true,
  user_actionable, LOCAL_ACTION, condition "The platform network adapter could
  not be opened". So an EAGAIN or EWOULDBLOCK on a socket that would succeed on
  the next poll arrives at the core labelled a permanent, user-fixable failure to
  open the adapter. It is not any of those four things.

  Amendment 1 added 21 TRANSIENT PLATFORM.* codes and not one of them can carry
  this: every one is a lifecycle, process or service event (PLATFORM.SUSPENDED,
  PLATFORM.LIFECYCLE.*, PLATFORM.SERVICE.*, four PLATFORM.EMBEDDED.*). The three
  closest codes anywhere in the registry were checked by name and all three are
  dishonest for it — PLATFORM.EMBEDDED.NETIFD_TEARDOWN names a specific OpenWrt
  event, RESOURCE.QUOTA.HANDSHAKE_RATE_LIMITED is gateway admission control, and
  STORE.KEYSTORE_LOCKED is a store state rather than a call outcome. Borrowing any
  of them would misattribute the condition to a domain that did not produce it.

  WHY IT BECAME URGENT RATHER THAN LATENT. PlatformError carried an
  is_retryable() predicate that read the variant's mapped class, so it answered
  false for the one variant whose name said otherwise. Every adapter had already
  noticed and routed around it, and five carried a tripwire test pinning the
  defect. That predicate is now DELETED — docs/reliability.md §3.1 says the retry
  policy, the backoff regime and the circuit breaker are driven by class, "never
  guessed from an error type", so a predicate on the enum was a second retry
  authority standing beside §6's governor. Deleting it was right, and it makes
  the mapping the ONLY retry authority left. twinvpn-session's class_admissible
  reads code.class() to decide which codes a state may carry, and PERSISTENT is
  admissible in BLOCKED — so with no honest TRANSIENT code, a recoverable syscall
  can be recorded as a blocking condition. The class is now load-bearing in a way
  it was not when W-40 was first filed.

WHY IT IS COMPATIBLE (§3 step 5):
  Purely additive, and additive in the one direction the registry is designed
  for. Reason codes travel the wire as STRINGS, so a reader that meets
  PLATFORM.ADAPTER_BUSY handles it exactly as it already handles any unknown
  code, using the carried attributes per ADR-0015 rule 5. No field number, no
  enum value, no wire format, no generated binding and no existing entry moved.
  The closed set of sixteen domains is unchanged. Nothing was deprecated,
  retired or renamed, so no S-37 compatibility event arises.

  The one wire-visible consequence is intended: SchemaDescriptor's
  reason_registry_version, generated from this file, goes 2 -> 3. That is what
  the field is for.

WHY THE NAME IS A CONDITION AND NOT A POLICY (ADR-0015 §11.2):
  Not PLATFORM.SYSCALL_RETRYABLE. "Retryable" is the answer the class carries,
  and reliability.md §3.1 is explicit that retry policy is read from class and
  never guessed elsewhere — a code whose NAME asserts the policy invites exactly
  the second authority that was just deleted. ADAPTER_BUSY names what the adapter
  reported and lets TRANSIENT carry what to do about it, and it pairs with
  ADAPTER_UNAVAILABLE: could not complete the call now, versus could not be
  opened at all.

APPROVED BY (§3 step 6): the repository owner, explicitly, on 2026-08-28, after
being shown that no existing code could honestly carry the condition and that
closing it required re-opening the freeze.

STILL OPEN after this amendment: the twinvpn-platform mapping itself. Registering
the code does not remap PlatformError::Transient onto it; that is a code change
in the five adapters and their tripwire tests, and W-40 closes only when both
halves have landed.

